// Live media has no root password, so polkit prompts cannot be answered.
// The original rule covered org.freedesktop.locale1.* (system keyboard/locale
// layout), but the installer also uses org.freedesktop.policykit.exec via
// pkexec. Other live helpers can request still more actions. Allow every
// polkit action unconditionally in the disposable live session only; do not
// depend on a username or "active" session flag, since KDE/KISS helpers may
// call D-Bus under a different account.
//
// The 00- prefix makes this authoritative: polkit reads rules in lexical
// order and stops at the first rule that returns a result, before Fedora's
// later rules can ask for authentication. A matching legacy .pkla is also
// installed as a fallback. These files go into the disposable live root only,
// not an installed system.
polkit.addRule(function(action, subject) {
    return polkit.Result.YES;
});
